          "guid": "ms2xqizxndslrpct",
          "message": {
            "text": "The fifteen tests that asserted \"no warning under NODE_ENV=production\" were testing the gate this change removes, so each was restated as a production-SHAPE assertion through this helper rather than deleted.\n\nThe distinction matters: they now drive the same public API (mount, defineStore, signal) with the hooks UNINSTALLED, which is what production actually is after KF-429. That is a stronger claim than the old one — it exercises the core-to-warner seam rather than a boolean inside the warner — and it keeps the behavior covered instead of trading a stale test for a coverage hole.\n\nTwo KERFDEV=true tests went the other way and now assert the inverse: an installed warner fires even under NODEENV=production. Those pin the property that replaced the gate.\n\nOne genuinely internal case (dev-invariants) could not be restated this way — the checker still works when called directly, since that is the point of the seam — so it asserts the empty hook slots instead.\n",
            "markdown": "The fifteen tests that asserted \"no warning under NODE_ENV=production\" were testing the gate this change removes, so each was restated as a production-SHAPE assertion through this helper rather than deleted.\n\nThe distinction matters: they now drive the same public API (`mount`, `defineStore`, `signal`) with the hooks UNINSTALLED, which is what production actually is after KF-429. That is a stronger claim than the old one — it exercises the core-to-warner seam rather than a boolean inside the warner — and it keeps the behavior covered instead of trading a stale test for a coverage hole.\n\nTwo `KERF_DEV=true` tests went the other way and now assert the inverse: an installed warner fires even under `NODE_ENV=production`. Those pin the property that replaced the gate.\n\nOne genuinely internal case (`dev-invariants`) could not be restated this way — the checker still works when called directly, since that is the point of the seam — so it asserts the empty hook slots instead.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tests/helpers/dev-shape.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 16,
                  "endLine": 23,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/** Uninstall every dev hook — kerf behaves exactly as it does in a production bundle. */\nexport function enterProductionShape(): void {\n  clearDevHooks();\n}\n\n/** Reinstall the standard dev bundle, undoing `enterProductionShape()`. */\nexport function restoreDevelopmentShape(): void {\n  installDevHooks(DEV_HOOKS);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
